>> title: Century Egg and Amaranth Soup
>> category: Soups
>> tags: century egg, amaranth, garlic, cantonese, quick soup, weeknight, stovetop
>> counters: The Soup Pot
>> aka: 皮蛋莧菜湯, pei daan jin coi tong, pei dan yin choi tong, century egg and amaranth soup, preserved egg and Chinese spinach soup, 滾湯, gwan tong
>> servings: 4
>> time: 20 min
>> slack: narrow — the amaranth gives its colour up in about three minutes, and the pot is grey-green by ten
>> step.1: Ten minutes and it comes out bright pink: the amaranth bleeds its colour into the broth.
>> step.2: fry the garlic in oil, 2 min
>> step.3: boil 5 min with the century eggs
>> step.4: stir the amaranth in, 3 min
>> step.5: season at the end

Ten minutes, and it comes out bright pink.

Fry @garlic{5%cloves}(smashed, left whole) in @vegetable oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) in a #soup pot{} ~fry{2%min}, until it is pale gold and no further — garlic that browns turns the whole bowl bitter.

Boil @&(~1)fried garlic{} with @water{5%cups}(1.2 L) and @century eggs{2}(pei daan; shelled and quartered — they go in early and half-dissolve into the broth, which is where the savour comes from) ~boil{5%min}.

Stir @amaranth{1%lb}(450 g; jin coi, leaves and tender stems) into @&(~1)soup{} and ~stir{3%min}, until it has wilted right down and the broth has turned pink.

Season @&(~1)soup{} with @kosher salt{1%tsp} and @white pepper{1/4%tsp}.
